    ],
    "justification": "The cell factorizations \\(z_{\\ell\\mathrm N}=a q_\\ell(1-e_\\ell)\\) and \\(z_{\\ell y}=a q_\\ell e_\\ell p_\\ell^y(1-p_\\ell)^{1-y}\\) recover every primitive coordinate, so direct substitution identifies the simplex and law-indexed formulas.",
    "gap": "Tan (2025) indexes the endpoint by the observed law but does not give a seven-cell simplex extension for every binary rational branch.",
    "consumer": "It makes the empirical plug-in map and every gradient in the multiplier envelope functions of the same multinomial probability vector.",
    "proof_tex": "For a law \\(P\\in\\mathcal M_\\eta\\), the seven cell probabilities factor as\n\\[\n z_\\varnothing=1-a,\\qquad\n z_{\\ell\\mathrm N}=a q_\\ell(1-e_\\ell),\\qquad\n z_{\\ell y}=a q_\\ell e_\\ell p_\\ell^y(1-p_\\ell)^{1-y}.\n\\]\nEvery factor is positive by \\(\\mathrm{ass{:}eta\\text{-}interior}\\).  Hence\n\\[\n d_\\ell=z_{\\ell\\mathrm N}+z_{\\ell0}+z_{\\ell1}=a q_\\ell,\\qquad\n m_\\ell=z_{\\ell0}+z_{\\ell1}=a q_\\ell e_\\ell,\\qquad\n z_{\\ell1}=a q_\\ell e_\\ell p_\\ell.\n\\]\nThe coordinate definitions therefore give\n\\[\n a(z)=a,\\quad q_\\ell(z)=q_\\ell,\\quad e_\\ell(z)=e_\\ell,\\quad p_\\ell(z)=p_\\ell,\n\\]\nwhich proves the asserted identity for \\(\\psi(z)\\).  Direct substitution of these seven equalities into every formula in \\(\\mathrm{def{:}seven\\text{-}cell\\text{-}simplex\\text{-}extensions}\\) gives, successively,\n\\[\n \\widetilde r_{\\ell\\beta}^s(z)=r_{\\ell\\beta}^s,\\quad\n \\widetilde t_{\\ell\\beta}^s(z)=t_{\\ell\\beta}^s,\\quad\n \\widetilde h_\\beta(z)=h_\\beta,\\quad\n \\widetilde f_\\beta^s(z)=f_\\beta^s(P).\n\\]\nThe same substitution in the compact envelope formulas yields \\(\\widetilde F_s(z)=F_s(P)\\).  Finally, the sharp-frontier theorem and the weak branch rules imply equality with every branch in \\(\\mathcal B_s(P)\\).  Because tied affine pieces agree at their common face and the final expression is independent of \\(h\\) when its two stratum values tie, this conclusion includes every active tie.",
